#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059452 :question/id #uuid "14e05d4f-373c-5d1f-aa59-7ee52466480e" :question/math-academy-id "e-14762" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\left| {\\begin{array}{ccc}0 & - 3 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8 \\\\ - 6 & - 12 & 1\\end{array}}\n\\right|.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & =0\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 8 \\\\ -12 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-(-3)\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+6\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0(8+96)+3(8+48)+6(-96+48) \\\\  & =0+3\\cdot 56+6\\cdot (-48) \\\\  & =168-288 \\\\  & =-120\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059453 :question/id #uuid "d7516cec-bd96-59db-98cd-5d82e41fa719" :question/math-academy-id "e-14763" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $A$ given below?\n\n- $\\det(A) = 0$\n\n- $A$ is **not** a singular matrix\n\n- $A$ is a singular matrix\n\n$$\nA={\\left[ \\begin{array}{ccc}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(0-4)-2(7-3)+3(4-0) \\\\  & =-4-2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-4-8+12 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(A)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059454 :question/id #uuid "7780340c-43d6-5d38-9270-865914098218" :question/math-academy-id "e-14764" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of  $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ is $2,$ find the value of the constant $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & =3\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}k & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}k & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3(12-10)-1(3k-0)+2(2k-0) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 3k+2\\cdot 2k \\\\  & =6-3k+4k \\\\  & =k+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $2,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k+6 & =2 \\\\ k & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059543 :question/id #uuid "1ab8245a-39fb-5633-b5ff-865ab17dbfb9" :question/math-academy-id "e-4323" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 0,-0.4,11 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 2,5,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =0\\cdot 2+(-0.4)\\cdot 5+11\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =0-2+22 \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059544 :question/id #uuid "dfc10727-c0d7-5b83-a4f6-afe3eb4831cd" :question/math-academy-id "e-4324" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a} = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}4 \\\\ - 2 \\\\ 1\\end{array} \\right]}$ and $\\mathbf{b} = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ t\\end{array} \\right]}$. Given that $\\mathbf{a} \\perp \\mathbf{b}$, find the value of $t$." :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{a} \\perp \\mathbf{b}$ ($\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are perpendicular) if and only if $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot t \\\\  & =-8-10+t \\\\  & =t-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ t-18 & =0 \\\\ t & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc68d302-4e05-53f4-a13b-62357c5a7653" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439477} {:answer/id #uuid "3bd87d1e-fd23-5dab-bc43-900e69f9433c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439478}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439477} :answer-field/id #uuid "91107b81-23d7-5b15-b57e-bf4ab1565fe8" :answer-field/key "$det(M)=10$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440096} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70ca64ce-81b4-5636-ba58-791451017b65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439479} {:answer/id #uuid "e05c2887-d7f6-57d2-a4c2-2f2da18a616f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439480}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439479} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2548bbb-9529-57ff-80c9-7eb2135baee7" :answer-field/key "$det(M)=-5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440097} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b319f9de-b31e-5b7f-b008-19047e4bc681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439481} {:answer/id #uuid "7743ec0d-8e7c-52c8-b5bf-a2c3ff1639ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439482}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439482} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3fd9d3c-6b34-5cd5-b3aa-e7329f24b386" :answer-field/key "$M$ is a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440098} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8899c4e3-2645-5f8b-9127-fbf8c6f48ee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667932} {:answer/id #uuid "478db39d-a240-5926-ab48-11c8e190272d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667933}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186667932} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae205eab-db1e-56c2-ac7d-5bc619d0d0ac" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668243}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d0d9bc49-c94e-5174-9068-2abf75c42684" :question/math-academy-id "q-128490" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $M$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 4\\end{vmatrix}+\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}(12-15)-0+\\frac{1}{3}(0+9\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\cdot (-3)+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =-3\\sqrt{5}+3\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(M)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement “$M$ is a singular matrix” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060030 